<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-notebook – R</title><link>https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/tags/r/</link><description>Recent content in R on go-notebook</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/tags/r/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>R cells</title><link>https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/r/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/r/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;```r&lt;/code&gt; block is an R cell (parsed since go-notebook v0.8.0, run since
v0.10.0). The R is &lt;a href="https://github.com/go-embedded-r/r" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-embedded-r&lt;/a&gt;, a
pure-Go R: go-notebook starts no external &lt;code&gt;R&lt;/code&gt;. Its parser checks the cell and
its evaluator runs it. Since v0.12.0 every R cell is bounded (see
&lt;a href="#limits"&gt;Limits&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-r" data-lang="r"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;3.4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;1.9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;5.6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="running"&gt;Running&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="running"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#running" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One environment.&lt;/strong&gt; The R cells of a notebook share one global environment,
so a variable assigned in one cell is there in the next, as in an R console.
A cell re-runs only when it or an R cell it reads changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output.&lt;/strong&gt; What a cell prints is its output, as an R console shows it:
&lt;code&gt;print&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;cat&lt;/code&gt;, and the value of every visible top-level expression. An
invisible value (&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- 1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;invisible(x)&lt;/code&gt;) prints nothing. &lt;code&gt;message()&lt;/code&gt; output
and the cell&amp;rsquo;s warnings go to the standard error, the warnings in R&amp;rsquo;s own form
(&lt;code&gt;Warning message:&lt;/code&gt; then &lt;code&gt;In f(x) : text&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;Warning messages:&lt;/code&gt; and a numbered
line each when there are several). An error fails the cell as
&lt;code&gt;Error in f(x) : text&lt;/code&gt;, after the output written before it, and the cells that
read it do not run. A cell that goes over a limit fails the same way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A cell shows text only, no figure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="limits"&gt;Limits&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="limits"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#limits" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A notebook may come from anyone, so each R cell runs with its own bounds:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Limit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Ends a cell with&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;512 MiB of vectors allocated in total over the cell, garbage included&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: memory limit exceeded: more than 536870912 bytes of vectors allocated&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;steps (calls plus loop iterations)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;50 million&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: evaluation step limit reached&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;30 s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;stopped: the R cell ran longer than 30s, the limit&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The step count is measured: &lt;code&gt;for (i in 1:n) s &amp;lt;- s + i&lt;/code&gt; stops at 16,666,666
iterations under 50 million steps, so a simulation of that size runs and an
endless loop ends in seconds. The session and its variables survive a limit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A program that embeds the kernel can change them with &lt;code&gt;kernel.Options.R&lt;/code&gt;: a
zero field is the default, and &lt;code&gt;-1&lt;/code&gt; is no bound. &lt;code&gt;--timeout&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--memory&lt;/code&gt;
apply to R cells as to every cell, and they kill the worker, session
included.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="parsing"&gt;Parsing&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="parsing"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#parsing" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;An R cell is parsed by go-embedded-r&amp;rsquo;s port of R 4.6&amp;rsquo;s grammar, which gives
the same trees and tokens as R 4.6.2 on all of R&amp;rsquo;s own &lt;code&gt;src/library&lt;/code&gt; and
&lt;code&gt;tests&lt;/code&gt; (932 files). A syntax error is reported at the notebook&amp;rsquo;s line and
column, with R&amp;rsquo;s own message:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```r
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-console" data-lang="console"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="gp"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; notebook run broken.md
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 0 (line 4, not run)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; error: 5:8: cell 0: syntax error: unexpected symbol
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;notebook: 1 cell(s) failed
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The parse is bounded (4 MiB per cell, a nesting depth of 1000, a million
nodes), so a notebook from anyone cannot make it run long or exhaust memory;
a cell over the limits fails with a message saying so.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="names"&gt;Names&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="names"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#names" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;An R cell joins the &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/cells/"&gt;rules of cells&lt;/a&gt; and the dependency graph. Its
names follow R&amp;rsquo;s scoping at the top level of the environment the cell runs in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Construct&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the notebook&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x = v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;v -&amp;gt; x&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;x&amp;quot; &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;assign(&amp;quot;x&amp;quot;, v)&lt;/code&gt; with a literal name&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x$a &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x[i] &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;names(x) &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;, and reads the &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; it modifies&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (i in s)&lt;/code&gt; at the top level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;f &amp;lt;- function(…) …&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;f = \(…) …&lt;/code&gt; at the top level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines the function &lt;code&gt;f&lt;/code&gt;: it stays R&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a free variable of the cell, or of a function&amp;rsquo;s body, that the cell does not assign&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a use: the cell depends on the cell that defines it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the parameters and local assignments of a function, and what &lt;code&gt;local()&lt;/code&gt; assigns&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;stay inside it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic cells.&lt;/strong&gt; Some R cannot be analysed from its text: &lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;&amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;,
&lt;code&gt;assign&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;get&lt;/code&gt; with a computed name, &lt;code&gt;eval&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;parse&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;attach&lt;/code&gt;,
&lt;code&gt;library&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;require&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;environment&amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;. Such a cell is &lt;strong&gt;dynamic&lt;/strong&gt;: it depends
on every cell before it, and every later cell that reads a name depends on
it, so nothing it may define is missed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R variables stay in R.&lt;/strong&gt; They are not shared with Go, Ruby, Julia or C cells
in either direction yet: a Go cell that reads an R name finds it undefined,
and an R cell does not see a Go variable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="in-the-browser"&gt;In the browser&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="in-the-browser"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#in-the-browser" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/playground/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;playground&lt;/a&gt; does not run R
cells: its WebAssembly cores do not link the evaluator. It parses and checks
them: the + menu and the cell&amp;rsquo;s language menu offer R, its badge reads
&lt;strong&gt;R · not runnable yet&lt;/strong&gt;, a syntax error is shown at its line in R&amp;rsquo;s words,
and the cells that read it are blocked, in the page&amp;rsquo;s neutral style and not as
failures. Run the notebook with &lt;code&gt;notebook run&lt;/code&gt; to execute its R cells.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>